  "figma read": {
    "help": "exit 0
Read a shallow design-file tree or a single node.

USAGE
  teamhub figma read <file-key|url> [flags]
  teamhub figma read --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --node <value>                Read one node; a URL may include the node-id.
  --depth <value>               Tree depth 1–5; default 1.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus File info and a depth-limited design node tree.

Figma Design only; FigJam, Slides, whole-file export, and PDF merge are out of scope.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub figma read 'https://www.figma.com/design/FILE_KEY/Design'

LEARN MORE
  teamhub figma --help
  teamhub figma read --schema --json
