  "gcal create": {
    "help": "exit 0
Create a meeting and notify attendees.

USAGE
  teamhub gcal create <title> --start <RFC3339> [--end <RFC3339> | --duration <minutes>] [flags]
  teamhub gcal create --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --calendar <value>            Calendar ID; default primary.
  --content <value>             Event description; exclusive with --file.
  --file <value>                UTF-8 description file; - reads stdin.
  --start <value>               RFC3339 start time.
  --end <value>                 RFC3339 end time; exclusive with --duration.
  --duration <value>            Duration in minutes, 1–1440; default 30.
  --attendee <value>            Attendee email; repeatable; at most 50.
  --location <value>            Location; at most 1000 characters.
  --meet                        Request a Google Meet link.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus The event after create, plus a meeting link when the provider returns one.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gcal create 'Project sync' --start 2026-10-19T10:00:00-04:00 --duration 30 --attendee alice@example.invalid --meet

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gcal --help
  teamhub gcal create --schema --json
",
