  "gcal list": {
    "help": "exit 0
List events for a day or a time window.

USAGE
  teamhub gcal list [flags]
  teamhub gcal list --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --calendar <value>            Calendar ID; default primary.
  --limit <value>               1–100 items per page; default 20.
  --cursor <value>              Cursor from the previous page; keep the same account and filters.
  --date <value>                today / tomorrow / YYYY-MM-DD; default today.
  --from <value>                RFC3339 start time; use together with --to.
  --to <value>                  RFC3339 end time, exclusive of this instant.
  --timezone <value>            IANA time zone for date mode; default calendar time zone.
  --query <value>               Event keyword; at most 1000 characters.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Event IDs, titles, start/end times, and next-page cursor.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gcal list --date tomorrow --timezone America/New_York

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gcal --help
  teamhub gcal list --schema --json
