  "gcal update": {
    "help": "exit 0
Update a single meeting and notify attendees.

USAGE
  teamhub gcal update <event-id> [flags]
  teamhub gcal update --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --calendar <value>            Calendar ID; default primary.
  --content <value>             Event description; exclusive with --file.
  --file <value>                UTF-8 description file; - reads stdin.
  --title <value>               New title; at most 500 characters.
  --start <value>               New start time; must be used with --end.
  --end <value>                 New end time; must be used with --start.
  --add-attendee <value>        Add one email; repeatable.
  --remove-attendee <value>     Remove one email; repeatable; cannot remove the organizer.
  --location <value>            New location.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus The event and attendees after update.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gcal update event_example --title 'Project sync (rescheduled)' --add-attendee bob@example.invalid

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gcal --help
  teamhub gcal update --schema --json
