  "gdrive upload": {
    "help": "exit 0
Upload one local regular file as a new remote file.

USAGE
  teamhub gdrive upload --file <path> --folder <id> [flags]
  teamhub gdrive upload --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --folder <value>              Existing parent folder ID; defaults to the root.
  --name <value>                Remote file name; defaults to the local basename.
  --file <value>                Local regular file; stdin is rejected.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus The remote file after name, size, and target folder are verified.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gdrive upload --file ./proposal.pdf --folder folder_example

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gdrive --help
  teamhub gdrive upload --schema --json
