  "github read": {
    "help": "exit 0
Read an issue or pull request with all its comments; a pull request also lists its changed files.

USAGE
  teamhub github read <owner/name#number|url> [flags]
  teamhub github read --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Issue or pull request body and comments; a pull request adds its branches, merge state, and changed files, each list with a completeness flag.

Reads up to 1,000 comments and 1,000 changed files and reports whether each list is complete; review comments and diffs are out of scope.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub github read 'https://github.com/octo-org/api/pull/42'

LEARN MORE
  teamhub github --help
  teamhub github read --schema --json
