  "gmail canvas-draft": {
    "help": "exit 0
Save the canvas as a Gmail draft with images in the body and file blocks attached; does not send.

USAGE
  teamhub gmail canvas-draft <document-id> [--update <draft-id>] [--to <email> ...] [--cc <email> ...] [--subject <text>] [flags]
  teamhub gmail canvas-draft --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --update <value>              Update the same draft instead of creating a new one.
  --to <value>                  Recipient; repeatable. Reads the canvas to field when omitted.
  --cc <value>                  Cc; repeatable. Reads the canvas cc field when omitted.
  --subject <value>             Subject with no line breaks. Reads the canvas subject when omitted.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus the operation result and receipt.

Images are sent as inline email images; total size must not exceed 5 MiB.
File blocks are sent as attachments; total size must not exceed 15 MiB.
Send with teamhub gmail send --draft <draft-id>.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gmail canvas-draft document_example
  teamhub gmail canvas-draft document_example --update r-123

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gmail --help
  teamhub gmail canvas-draft --schema --json
