  "gmail download": {
    "help": "exit 0
Download selected attachments from a message to local files without overwriting.

USAGE
  teamhub gmail download <message-id> (--attachment <name> | --attachment-id <id>) --output <path> [flags]
  teamhub gmail download <message-id> --all --output <directory> [flags]
  teamhub gmail download --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --attachment <value>          Exact attachment name; use --attachment-id when names collide.
  --attachment-id <value>       Attachment ID from read; exclusive with name and --all.
  --all                         Download every regular-file attachment; skip inline images and non-file attachments.
  --output <value>              New file path for a single attachment; an existing directory with --all. Does not overwrite.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Message ID, saved attachment name/ID/absolute path/byte size/SHA-256, and skipped items.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gmail download message_example --attachment 'proposal.pdf' --output ./proposal.pdf
  teamhub gmail download message_example --all --output ./attachments

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gmail --help
  teamhub gmail download --schema --json
