  "gmail read": {
    "help": "exit 0
Read a message, thread, or known draft without changing read state.

USAGE
  teamhub gmail read <message-id> [--thread] [flags]
  teamhub gmail read --draft <draft-id> [flags]
  teamhub gmail read --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --limit <value>               1–100 items per page; default 20.
  --cursor <value>              Cursor returned by the previous page; keep the same account and filters.
  --thread                      Read the containing thread.
  --draft <value>               Read by draft ID; exclusive with the positional argument and thread options.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Message body, recipients, and attachments; thread mode includes the message list, draft mode includes the draft ID.

Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub gmail read message_example --thread
  teamhub gmail read --draft draft_example

LEARN MORE
  teamhub gmail --help
  teamhub gmail read --schema --json
",
