  "message card": {
    "help": "exit 0
teamhub message card [--thread <id>] [--kind profile] --title <text> (--content <text> | --file <path|->) [--attach <path> ...] [--document <id> ...]
Send one light card to the Room or one of its Threads: a title, a one-line result and files. Deliver a finished background Task's result with it, or point out something the user must notice; reply in ordinary messages otherwise.

Options:
  --thread <value>  Bare Thread ID inside the configured Room.
  --title <value>  The card's title: one line, at most 120 characters.
  --kind <value>  Only profile: marks the delivery of the Human's Personal Profile.
  --content <value>  Inline body text; never read as a path. Outside code, \\n and \\t become a line break and a tab, and \\\\ becomes \\ (write \\\\n for a literal \\n; inside shell double quotes type \\\\\\\\n). Code and --file bodies are never decoded.
  --file <value>  Read a UTF-8 body file; - consumes stdin (multi-line text, e.g. a heredoc).
  --attach <value>  Local file published with the card, e.g. from ./playground/<task-id>/; repeatable, no directories.
  --document <value>  Existing Document ID shown on the card; repeatable.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
The body is a one-line result kept with the card; the Web shows only the title and files (and the body of a profile card). Put details in the files, and say what the user should add or check in one ordinary message after the card.
--content/--file support [@Name](user:actor_id) or [@Name](agent:actor_id).
A failed Task is not delivered as a card; say what happened in an ordinary message.
Resource paths cannot use stdin or URLs. Publication and message commit are atomic.
Examples:
teamhub message card --title "Competitor comparison" --content "A cut its enterprise price 15%; B moved its launch to early November." --attach ./playground/task_8f2c/comparison.xlsx
",
