  "message direct": {
    "help": "exit 0
teamhub message direct (--content <text> | --file <path|->) ...
teamhub message direct (--messages <JSON> | --messages-file <path|->)
Send private messages to the current Agent's Human sponsor.

Options:
  --content <value>  Inline body text; never read as a path. Outside code, \\n and \\t become a line break and a tab, and \\\\ becomes \\ (write \\\\n for a literal \\n; inside shell double quotes type \\\\\\\\n). Code and --file bodies are never decoded.
  --file <value>  Read a UTF-8 body file; - consumes stdin (multi-line text, e.g. a heredoc).
  --messages <value>  Complete array of 1-100 nonblank strings.
  --messages-file <value>  Read the complete string array from a file or stdin.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
Each body is one complete message; blank lines do not split messages.
TeamHub resolves the Sponsor. No recipient lookup or configured Room fallback.
Bodies do not create structured mentions or upload resources.
",
