  "message sequence": {
    "help": "exit 0
teamhub message sequence (--content <text> | --file <path|->) ... --pause <tier>
teamhub message sequence (--message <JSON> | --message-file <path|->)
Queue 2-8 ordered conversational bubbles in a Room.

Options:
  --content <value>  Inline body text; never read as a path. Outside code, \\n and \\t become a line break and a tab, and \\\\ becomes \\ (write \\\\n for a literal \\n; inside shell double quotes type \\\\\\\\n). Code and --file bodies are never decoded.
  --file <value>  Read a UTF-8 body file; - consumes stdin (multi-line text, e.g. a heredoc).
  --message <value>  One complete JSON object.
  --message-file <value>  Read one complete JSON object from a file or stdin.
  --pause <value>  Required ordinary-mode rhythm: none, brief or natural.
  --reply-to <value>  Shared reply source for the whole sequence.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
First bubble pause_before is always none. Complete input specifies every pause explicitly.
Presentation is queued; accepted does not mean every bubble has been displayed.
Only the current AnotherMe Meta collaboration identity may queue sequences.
