  "notion append": {
    "help": "exit 0
Append content at the end of the page and keep the existing body.

USAGE
  teamhub notion append <page> [flags]
  teamhub notion append --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --content <value>             Body text; exclusive with --file; plain text by default.
  --file <value>                UTF-8 body file; - reads stdin.
  --markdown                    Use the common Markdown subset validated by the backend.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Append receipt plus read-back verification and completeness.

A fragment in a page URL does not narrow the read or edit range; databases and whole-page overwrite are out of scope.
The external write waits for the sponsor to approve a confirmation card in the chat; TeamHub then runs it and sends you the result, or the denial and its reason.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub notion append '<page-url>' --content 'Follow-up: acceptance completed on Friday.'

LEARN MORE
  teamhub notion --help
  teamhub notion append --schema --json
",
