  "outlook send": {
    "help": "exit 0
Send a new message or an existing draft.

USAGE
  teamhub outlook send --to <email> --subject <text> (--content <text> | --file <path|->) [--markdown | --html] [--attach <path>] [flags]
  teamhub outlook send --draft <draft-id> [flags]
  teamhub outlook send --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --attach <value>              Attach a local regular file; repeatable; stdin is rejected.
  --content <value>             Body text; exclusive with --file.
  --file <value>                UTF-8 body file; - reads stdin, not an attachment.
  --markdown                    TeamHub converts Markdown to HTML on the backend.
  --html                        Use HTML body text as-is.
  --to <value>                  One bare email address; repeatable.
  --cc <value>                  One Cc email address; repeatable.
  --bcc <value>                 One Bcc email address; repeatable.
  --subject <value>             Subject with no line breaks.
  --draft <value>               Send a saved draft; exclusive with body, recipients, and format flags.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Upstream send-accepted receipt and any available message/thread IDs; this does not mean delivery.

The external write waits for the sponsor to approve a confirmation card in the chat; TeamHub then runs it and sends you the result, or the denial and its reason.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub outlook send --to alice@example.invalid --subject 'Project update' --markdown --file ./weekly.md --attach ./proposal.pdf
  teamhub outlook send --draft draft_example

LEARN MORE
  teamhub outlook --help
  teamhub outlook send --schema --json
",
