",
  },
  "slack react": {
    "help": "exit 0
Add an emoji reaction; --remove only removes your own reaction.

USAGE
  teamhub slack react <emoji> (--channel <#name> | --channel-id <id>) --message-id <id> [--remove] [flags]
  teamhub slack react <emoji> --message-url <url> [--remove] [flags]
  teamhub slack react --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --channel <value>             Exact #channel name.
  --channel-id <value>          Conversation ID; skip name discovery.
  --message-id <value>          Exact message ID to react to.
  --message-url <value>         Slack HTTPS message URL.
  --remove                      Remove your own reaction.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus The actual message target, emoji name, and add/remove receipt.

Common emoji names: 👍 thumbsup · 👎 thumbsdown · ✅ white_check_mark · 👀 eyes · 🎉 tada · ❤️ heart · 🙏 pray · 🚀 rocket. Use the name without colons or the glyph; known workspace custom names also work.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub slack react thumbsup --channel-id C012EXAMPLE --message-id 1792039200.000100

LEARN MORE
  teamhub slack --help
  teamhub slack react --schema --json
",
