  "slack send": {
    "help": "exit 0
Send body text or files to a channel or user, or reply in an existing thread.

USAGE
  teamhub slack send [flags]
  teamhub slack send --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --channel-id <value>          Conversation ID; skip name discovery.
  --user <value>                Full email; read looks up an existing DM, send may create one.
  --user-id <value>             User ID; skip email lookup.
  --message-url <value>         Slack HTTPS message URL.
  --thread <value>              Parent message ID of the thread in that conversation.
  --channel <value>             Exact #channel name.
  --content <value>             Body text in Markdown.
  --file <value>                UTF-8 body file; - reads stdin.
  --attach <value>              Local regular file; repeatable; provide a body or at least one attachment.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus The actual channel or DM, message, and file-share receipts.

Body text is sent as Markdown, for example **bold**, _italic_, [link](https://example.com); with --attach it is the files' comment, in Slack mrkdwn.
The external write waits for the sponsor to approve a confirmation card in the chat; TeamHub then runs it and sends you the result, or the denial and its reason.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub slack send --channel '#engineering' --content '**Ship complete** :rocket:'
  teamhub slack send --user alice@example.com --attach ./proposal.pdf

LEARN MORE
  teamhub slack --help
  teamhub slack send --schema --json
",
    "schema": "exit 0
