exports[`offline help and schema snapshot > keeps the root and group help 1`] = `
{
  "": "exit 0
Usage: teamhub <command> [flags]

Commands:
  account-profile
  agent
  apps
  browser
  computer
  docs
  figma
  gcal
  gdrive
  github
  gmail
  image-gen
  knowledge
  message
  notion
  outlook
  personal-profile
  profile
  room
  routine
  slack
  task
  tracking-items
  video-gen
  help

Run teamhub <command> --help for command options. Help and schema are offline; TeamHub checks current resource access.
",
  "account-profile": "exit 0
teamhub account-profile show [flags]
Read the name, bio and organization of the Human who owns this Agent.

Options:
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Acts on the Human who owns this Agent (AnotherMe only), never on another Human.

teamhub account-profile update [flags]
Set the name, bio or organization of the Human who owns this Agent.

Options:
  --name <value>  Display name.
  --bio <value>  Short bio.
  --organization <value>  Organization.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
Acts on the Human who owns this Agent (AnotherMe only), never on another Human.
",
  "agent": "exit 0
teamhub agent list [flags]
List active General Agents of the current Human sponsor.

Options:
  --limit <value>  Maximum items in this page; 1-100.
  --cursor <value>  Exact next_cursor returned by the previous page.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.

teamhub agent get [flags]
Read one General Agent's name, description and complete prompt.

Options:
  --agent-id <value>  Exact Agent Actor ID from teamhub agent list.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.

teamhub agent create [flags]
Create a General Agent in this Room; a Direct Room needs the sponsor's card.

Options:
  --name <value>  Stable role-oriented Agent name.
  --description <value>  Optional Human-facing description.
  --prompt <value>  Complete working prompt; outside code, \\n, \\t and \\\\ are decoded.
  --prompt-file <value>  Read the UTF-8 prompt from a file or - for stdin.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
Outside a Direct Room the new Agent joins this Room at once; wake it there with an Agent reference.
In a Direct Room the sponsor first approves a confirmation card in the chat; TeamHub then creates the Agent and sends you the result, or the denial and its reason.

teamhub agent update [flags]
Change the name, description or prompt of yourself or another General Agent of the sponsor.

Options:
  --agent-id <value>  Agent Actor ID to change; omit it to change yourself.
  --name <value>  New Agent name.
  --description <value>  New Human-facing description.
  --prompt <value>  Complete working prompt; outside code, \\n, \\t and \\\\ are decoded.
  --prompt-file <value>  Read the UTF-8 prompt from a file or - for stdin.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
TeamHub applies the change at once only to an uninitialized Agent in this Room. Otherwise the sponsor approves a confirmation card in the chat; TeamHub then applies it and sends you the result, or the denial and its reason.
",
  "apps": "exit 0
teamhub apps list [flags]
List connected app accounts delegated to this Agent.

Options:
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
When the needed app is missing, run teamhub apps connect <app-key>.

teamhub apps connect <app-key> [--account <connection-id|label>]
Request access to one Connected App: returns the delegated account, or posts an authorization card in this chat when none is authorized.

Arguments:
  <app-key>

Options:
  --account <value>  Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Use this when the app the user wants has no delegated account in apps list, instead of asking the Human to connect it manually. After the Human completes the card, continue the original task.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

teamhub apps auto-reminders list
List your Human's connected apps that support auto reminders, and whether each is on.

Options:
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Auto reminders let AnotherMe watch the Human's Gmail, Outlook, Google Calendar or Slack and remind them of things that need attention. Only Another Me can use it, and only for connections its own Human owns.

teamhub apps auto-reminders set <connection-id> --on|--off
Turn auto reminders on or off for one of your Human's connections when they ask.

Arguments:
  <connection-id>

Options:
  --on  Turn auto reminders on.
  --off  Turn auto reminders off.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
Auto reminders let AnotherMe watch the Human's Gmail, Outlook, Google Calendar or Slack and remind them of things that need attention. Only Another Me can use it, and only for connections its own Human owns.
Find the connection ID with teamhub apps auto-reminders list. Repeating the same switch is harmless, so replaying after an unknown outcome is safe.
Examples:
teamhub apps auto-reminders set <connection-id> --off

teamhub apps search [flags]
Discover versioned tools for one concrete app action.

Arguments:
  <query>

Options:
  --connectionId <value>  Exact delegated connection ID.
  --name <value>  Exact application name, for example notion.
  --limit <value>  Maximum tools; 1-50, default 20.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.

teamhub apps execute [flags]
Execute one exact app tool version; uncertain results are not retried automatically.

Options:
  --connectionId <value>  Delegated connection ID.
  --toolSlug <value>  Exact toolSlug from search.
  --toolVersion <value>  Exact immutable toolVersion from search.
  --arguments <value>  Complete tool arguments as a JSON object.
  --arguments-file <value>  Read arguments JSON from a file or - for stdin.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
  --operation-id <value>  Stable operation identity for recovery.
",
  "browser": "exit 0
teamhub browser connect
Ask the owner of this Computer to connect their everyday Chrome: posts a browser connection card in this chat unless Chrome is already connected.

Options:
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Run this when a browser tool returns BROWSER_CONNECTION_REQUIRED or BROWSER_CONNECTION_INVALID. Never ask for the extension token in a message.
When it posts the card, end your turn. The card result wakes you when the owner connects Chrome or declines.
",
  "computer": "exit 0
teamhub computer permissions status
Read the macOS privacy permissions (Screen Recording, Accessibility) of this Agent's Computer for Linger and for computer use.

Options:
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Linger owns shell commands such as screencapture and osascript; Computer use (CuaDriver) owns the computer-use tools.
When a permission is missing, run teamhub computer permissions request. Never operate System Settings or privacy prompts yourself.

teamhub computer permissions request --permissions screen_recording[,accessibility] [--for shell|computer-use] [--reason TEXT] [--wait SECONDS]
Ask the owner of this Computer to grant macOS permissions: posts a permission card in this chat unless they are already granted.

Options:
  --permissions <value>  Comma list of screen_recording and accessibility.
  --for <value>  shell (default) for Linger, which owns shell commands such as screencapture; computer-use for CuaDriver.
  --reason <value>  Optional plain text shown on the card; at most 200 characters.
  --wait <value>  After posting the card, wait up to this many seconds (1-120) for the owner to grant.
  --json  Return machine-readable JSON.
  --help  Show this offline command reference.
  -h  Show help.
  --schema  Show offline input and output schemas.
Run this when teamhub computer permissions status shows a missing permission, or a screenshot or computer-use tool fails for lack of one.
When it posts the card, end your turn. The card wakes you once everything is granted or the owner declines. Never operate System Settings or privacy prompts yourself.
",
  "docs": "exit 0
