  "video-gen": "exit 0
Start a video generation job, look up model prices, or check a job and save its result.

USAGE
  teamhub video-gen --provider <provider> --model <model-id> --prompt <text> [flags]
  teamhub video-gen --provider <provider> --price [--model <model-id>] [flags]
  teamhub video-gen --provider <provider> --model <model-id> --job <job-id> [flags]
  teamhub video-gen --schema [--json]

FLAGS
  --provider <value>            fal or higgsfield; required.
  --model <value>               Provider model ID; required for generation and job lookup.
  --prompt <value>              What to generate; required for generation.
  --price                       Read model prices without starting a job; --model selects one model and its parameters.
  --job <value>                 Check an existing job once without submitting again; repeatable for Higgsfield.
  --set <value>                 Model parameter as field=value; repeatable. JSON values keep their types.
  --file <value>                Reference input as field=local-path; repeatable. Use a fal input field or a Higgsfield media role.
  --output <value>              Where finished results are saved: one to a new file, several to a new directory. Saved by the --job check that finds the job finished; never overwrites.
  --limit <value>               Price-list page size, 1-100, default 20.
  --cursor <value>              Continue the previous price-list page with the same provider and account.
  --account <value>             Select a connection ID or complete account label; when authorization is missing, an authorization card is shown in the chat.
  --json                        Print complete JSON instead of the default readable text.
  --schema                      Show offline input and output schemas without business arguments.
  --operation-id <value>        Stable identity for this operation; keep it when the outcome is unknown and do not blindly resend.

INHERITED FLAGS
  -h, --help                   Show help.

OUTPUT
  Shows the actual account, plus Actual object IDs, operation receipts, and verifiable state; upstream acceptance is not reported as final completion.

Generation spends the selected connected account's balance. --price returns fal unit prices; Higgsfield reports pricingStatus=unavailable because its model catalog exposes no price table. No estimate is substituted and no job starts.
Generation returns as soon as the provider accepts the job; it does not wait for the result. Run the returned nextCommand later to check the job once; it saves to --output when the job has finished. Never repeat a paid submission after an unknown outcome.
--price --model also shows model-specific parameters and reference inputs. Pass those parameters with --set and local reference files with --file.
A single result is saved as delivered under the requested name. A warning reports a mismatched file extension; no conversion is performed.
Help and schema are available offline; TeamHub checks current access at execution time.

EXAMPLES
  teamhub video-gen --provider higgsfield --model seedance_2_5 --prompt "camera slowly orbits the product" --file start_image=./bottle.png --set duration=5 --output ./orbit.mp4
  teamhub video-gen --provider fal --price

LEARN MORE
  teamhub  --help
  teamhub video-gen --schema --json
",
}
`;
